A||||12||JohnnyK||Trying to build a go-kart.||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||12-07-2000||04:31 PM||||Well, i'm buying the actual frame, 2 back wheels/axle/bearings off some guy in my class for 10 bucks. (well, comes with a 3.5 engine, but it's kind of dead, with no carb or anything). So I'm trying to find some assorted things for it. Mainly an engine (I'm pretty sure I can figure the steering out with a few bucks). My question is, where can I find a good motor for cheap? I can't really afford 200 bucks on a motor, or a used snowblower, etc. And I'm pretty sure I couldn't use a lawnmower engine since it's vertical (I have plenty of those). How about an outboard motor? Are those vertical or horizontal?||||reg||1
Z||000001||btoth||12-07-2000||05:35 PM||||When I was looking into building one (never did though) I saw at our local lawnmower repair place that they had vertical Briggs&Straton motors, but I think the cheepest one was around $100 and 5hp.  I wonder if you could use a mower off of a tiller (? one of those things that churns up dirt).  Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||12-07-2000||09:43 PM||||Some of my best racing engines came off of a tiller. You can buy them fairly cheap at yard sales and trade day places. I have even lucked up on a couple of dual bearing I/C engines on old tillers and brought them home for less than $50.||||reg||1
Z||000003||alpha||12-07-2000||10:02 PM|||| <A HREF="http://home.sprintmail.com/~fourays/family.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.sprintmail.com/~fourays/family.htm</A> <P>That guy built a cart with a vertical shaft engine...scroll to the bottom of the page.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://fiero.dhs.org/fiero/sig.jpg">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu">douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||zeusrekning||12-07-2000||10:21 PM||||I have a lot of parts just tell me what you need. From axles to flywheels.<BR>If you are interested in building a vertical shaft cart i have a foward reverse gearbox.<BR>I like off road carts and pushing those things backwards after going downhill into a tree sucks.||||reg||1
Z||000005||olympic||12-07-2000||11:15 PM||||  IF your just building it for fun look into using a liquid cooled snowmobile engine and centrifugal clutch!!!  That would be pretty insane with 50+ hp...lol||||reg||1
