Z||000008||JohnnyK||12-08-2000||03:51 PM||||Zeus: How much you wanna sell the engine and clutch for? (And maybe the tie rods)?||||reg||1
Z||000009||zeusrekning||12-08-2000||07:34 PM||||I'd be nice and send you parts to build an engine. I have a torque-a-verter.(This is like a variable speed transmission) They go for like $100-$150 new, I had to build a new part for it. The part that connects the two pullies was made of thin stampered steel and it bent, so i made a plate that is shaped like [  it goes under the engine then comes up and bolts to the head to hold the new bearing housing i made and i also made a stainless jackshaft cause the carbon steel one kept rusting.It is heavier but wont bend.<BR>Don't know what kinda shape the t-c is in but i'd get rid of it to.<BR>I wouldn't mind builing an engine for you if you don't know how . Just charge you the price of new gaskets and rings + shipping and mabey like 20 bucks for engine and labor.<BR>I'll give you some tie rods. they are nothing but two rods threaded on both ends.<BR>Mine may be bent have to look.<BR>not sure what i want for the t-c<BR>Let me see if i can find pics of my cart.||||reg||1
Z||000010||JohnnyK||12-09-2000||11:33 AM||||Thanks loads man! I got this 3.5 HP motor fired up (what a sissy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and I'm going to go to princess auto today to look for a centrifical clutch, and some ball joints for the end (and some rod to thread). Besides that, I think I just have to rebuild this old cart. I have a funny feeling 3.5 HP isn't going to push anything. I'll let ya know when I get back!||||reg||1
Z||000011||JohnnyK||12-09-2000||10:54 PM||||Nope.. The thing ddin't move at all. The clutch was just sparking. Shouldn't the engine stall instead though? Or do those clutches just slip instead of stalling.||||reg||1
Z||000012||KRMFiero||12-10-2000||01:11 AM||||Just thought i would tell you last year I made a go-cart, I got a Honda 175 CC dirtbike engine from a junk yard for 10$ (it ran), mounted it on a custom made engine mount (I should not have used fiber board, water stinks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> hah)    and well I had to face the eninge backwords, put a little sprocket on a 1" rod - the little spricket went to the engine sprocket and then the rod went accross to the other side of the go-kart and i had another sprocket which had the chain on going to the axle.... I cant really explain it but it was cool, VERY fast (5 speed transmition heheh)   but i made the whole ening mount out of fiberboard and i took it off road, went in a small pond (hydroplaned accross it) and when i was going back right before I went to go accross the pond again (about 3 foot deep) the fiberboard snaped, engine fell off, i costed into the water (ehh it sucked) I just left the frame there, took the eninge  and walked home... <BR>well the point of me saying that is umm i dont know probley I reccomed you use medal to mount your engine on hahah<P><BR>l8r<BR>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE<BR>Front - AudioBahn 4 x 10<BR>Headrest - AudioBahn 3 1/2<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
